{
  "dom_id": "step-q145041",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+2y}{2y+1}, & \\,0<x<1,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<\\frac{3}{4}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<\\frac{3}{4}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/4}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/4}\\frac{(2x+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})}{(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3/4}(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[{x}^{2}+x]_{0}^{3/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9}{16}+\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{21}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
